d frank  put forward they recognized the  marketing value of a rebranding so from  that point forward annie oakley was  billed as little sure shot with their  contract with the cell's brother's  circus expired frank and annie thought  that they would try to go for the big  time and in the world of travelling  shows there was no bigger than buffalo  bills while west oakley met with bill  cody and his business partner nate  salisbury in 1884 but she left  disappointed buffalo bill already had a  shooting act captain adam begardes and  his four young sons danny oakley was  still small-time compared to him so cody  had no reason to choose her but soon  enough they played her hand again in  late 1884 the steamboat carrying the  wild west crown equipment was heading to  new orleans when it collided with  another steamer and sank there were no  casualties but bergard has lost his  equipment and suffered some damage to  his equilibrium which never got better  in march 1885 he left buffalo bill's  show at that point oakley approached  cody again and offered to do three shows  for free as an audition and with nothing  to lose bill said well what the hell and  accept it  [Music]  ry with her first performance it became  immediately clear to bill cody that  annie oakley was destined to become a  star unsurprisingly bill signed her to a  deal immediately and the two embarked on  a 17-year long business relationship  that saw them travel up and down the  country as well as across the atlantic  to perform in front of the kings and  queens of europe becoming particularly  popular in england the prince of wales  even organized a shooting contest  between annie oakley and the grand duke  michael of russia who fancied himself  quite a marksman a contest that danny  obviously won oakley and cody got along  well for the most part and he described  buffalo bill as one of the nicest men in  the world while cody wrote of oakley  that she was the loveliest and truest  little woman both in h